From d8c6b11199a0063fbda1f2651c4aae49ac2eb3d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LiBr <me@nvme0n1p.dev>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 15:42:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 36/47] Z 6III: the top LCD -- the MCU's SPI2 by DMA, a 128x128
 memory LCD

The control panel on the right shoulder never showed anything: the body
MCU drives it over SPI2 by DMA, and nothing pulled that stream, so the
first transfer never completed. Followed through the MCU image:

  - the EXPEED sends the panel's content as state, not pixels: family 8
    kind 4, 192 bytes (with kind 1, 20 bytes of flags). The MCU's display
    task keeps it (sub_80327D8 -> 0x2001A9FA, event 8), checks its 83
    fields (sub_8030350), renders a 2048-byte frame from it with its own
    glyphs (sub_8030E0C) and hands that to sub_8032554, which compares it
    line by line with the last frame sent and packs only the lines that
    changed;
  - what it sends is the write protocol of a Sharp memory-in-pixel LCD:
    0x80 (M0, data update), then per line the gate address, 16 bytes and
    a dummy, a trailing dummy; at power-on 0x20 0x00 (M2, all clear,
    sub_8032058). The frame is 128 lines of 16 bytes and line i's address
    is table 0x8058A10[i] = bit-reversed 128 - i: a 128x128 panel taking
    its address LSB first, with the MCU's row 0 at its line 128;
  - HAL_SPI_Transmit_DMA (sub_804D580, from sub_8032704) on SPI2, DMA1
    stream 4, framed by an active-high chip select that the begin and end
    hooks move (sub_8032350 / sub_8032360: PA4), DISP raised once the
    clear is out (sub_8031FA8: PE8).

nikon-z63-stm32.h: an SPI can have a listening device (a "sink", no
MISO). With CR2.TXDMAEN it takes the armed stream's words itself, at its
own bit rate (CR1.BR from APB1/APB2, CR1.DFF), so TC and the firmware's
chip-select drop come when they would; DR writes reach the sink too. The
link's SPI1/SPI4 are untouched -- the board still clocks those.

nikon-z63-toplcd.h: the panel -- SCS, DISP, the three modes, its memory
-- publishing what it shows to -machine toplcd-live=<file> in
scanout-live's layout (128x128, white for a 1 bit, the panel's own
order; z63ui turns it a quarter clockwise, as it sits in the body).

One line is not the panel's: after the clear the MCU pulses PD11 for
1 ms and arms PD1 -- input, pull-up, EXTI rising (sub_8032690) -- and
sends no line until that edge sets 0x2001BB84 (sub_8032908 -> event 0x80
-> sub_8032264). Without it the packets queue, the queue stays full and
the task renders nothing more. A memory LCD has no output, so what drives
PD1 is not known; the pull-up and rising edge read like an open-drain
ready from the panel's supply. DECLARED: PD11's pulse pulls PD1 low and
it is let go 5 ms after the pulse ends.

Now the panel shows what the body's would: 1.6" F--, ISO-A 64000, the
release mode S, the mains-power icon and [-E-] for no card, updating as
the EXPEED's state changes (ISO-A 100 a little later, the exposure
readout gone when the meters time out). smoke.sh passes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
